Q: Graph API Unable to read JSON request payload A: <p>This error occurs because your payload isn't in a valid json format. You have to escape the quotation marks. Use <code>\&quot;</code> intead of <code>&quot;</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
   &quot;data&quot;: &quot;&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;The title attribute example&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;h3 title=\&quot;Hello HTML!\&quot;&gt;Titled head tag example&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&quot;
}
</code></pre>

Q: TreeView HierarchicalDataTemplate ItemsSource binding to self without a property path A: <p>That's one of those days you feel so dumb you want to just vanish.. I forgot <code>Binding</code>s are to be defined with care:</p>
<p>This changes the <code>source</code> to the <code>Control</code> that, as expected, is not a collection (but raises no error, which is not an issue in itself), hence no items to spawn whatsoever:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;TreeView ...&gt;
    &lt;TreeView.ItemTemplate&gt;
        &lt;HierarchicalDataTemplate 
            ItemsSource=&quot;{
                Binding RelativeSource={RelativeSource Self},
                UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}&quot;&gt;
                    ...
</code></pre>
<p><strong>The <code>Path=.</code> (dot) does instead keep the collection as the <code>source</code>:</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;TreeView ...&gt;
    &lt;TreeView.ItemTemplate&gt;
        &lt;HierarchicalDataTemplate 
            ItemsSource=&quot;{
                Binding Path=.,
                UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}&quot;&gt;
                    ...
</code></pre>
<p>same as writing:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;TreeView ...&gt;
    &lt;TreeView.ItemTemplate&gt;
        &lt;HierarchicalDataTemplate 
            ItemsSource=&quot;{
                Binding UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}&quot;&gt;
                    ...
</code></pre>
<p>or to be specific as mentioned by <strong>EldHasp</strong> (in comments <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79911462/2410892">in his answer below</a>):</p>
<pre><code>&lt;TreeView ...&gt;
    &lt;TreeView.ItemTemplate&gt;
        &lt;HierarchicalDataTemplate 
            ItemsSource=&quot;{
                Binding DataContext, RelativeSource={RelativeSource Self}}&quot;&gt;
                    ...
</code></pre>
<p>^^ <code>DataContext</code> being the collection itself (that's the one I'll use, thanks)</p>
<p>(Also as pointed out, <code>UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged</code> is of no effect whatsoever in this case: the <code>DataContext/collection</code> <em>is not a property of &quot;itself&quot;</em> since there is no <code>Path=</code> specifying the <code>DataContext</code> property member to monitor/hook to in the <code>ItemsSource</code> binding, therefore, no <code>PropertyChanged</code> will ever occur)</p>
<p>I looked for an issue where there was none. The classes and collections are fine, the interfaces are fine..  quite an epic oversight. Sorry for the trouble. Well, I'll be very wary every time I write <code>RelativeSource=...</code> from now on...</p>
<p><strong>It's all thanks to this answer in another question</strong> :</p>
<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/1906613/2410892">WPF Bind to itself, by Heinzi</a> :</p>
<p><em>... This sets the source to the control itself, so it will try to access property x of the UI control...</em></p>
<p>The upside is, now we can finalize the instanciable collections with proper serialization and deserialization implementations, <strong>seal them</strong>, then move on.</p>
